1
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,120
Hold on a little longer.

2
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,520
The glass elevator is just ahead.

3
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:44,520
We'll take it down the mountain

4
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:45,580
and enjoy the view.

5
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,200
Did you all bring your laptops?

6
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,040
Yes, we did.

7
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:49,400
Even though we're out for team building,

8
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,480
the work

9
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:51,680
must not be left behind. Didn't they say

10
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,360
something about enjoying
the natural scenery?

11
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,620
He's always like this.

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:55,960
It sounds nice to call it team building,

13
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,480
but it's actually just
an off-site meeting.

14
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:58,880
Yuan, let me take a picture of you.

15
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,360
Come on.

16
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:01,080
What's wrong?

17
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,519
Do we have to take
the glass elevator down?

18
00:01:04,519 --> 00:01:06,240
I'm really afraid of heights.

19
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,240
Look at you,

20
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:09,600
always messing up
everyone's plans with this stuff.

21
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,280
Just get over

22
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,640
minor issues like a fear of heights.

23
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,280
The elevator isn't dangerous.

24
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:16,760
Just close your eyes
if you're really scared.

25
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,080
Are you crying now?

26
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,170
Everyone else is fine, except you.

27
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,640
What do I always say?

28
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,200
We are a team,

29
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:25,320
and we need team spirit, right?

30
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,320
Girls are fragile by nature.

31
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:30,160
They cry over the smallest things.

32
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,800
Climbing up here was tiring enough.

33
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,320
If we all have to walk
down the mountain with you

34
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:35,120
because of your issues,

35
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,039
is that reasonable?

36
00:01:36,039 --> 00:01:37,240
Is that appropriate?

37
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,400
It's ridiculous.

38
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,160
We don't have much time to hang out,

39
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,320
so let's not waste it.

40
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,920
As a team member,

41
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,240
you shouldn't be so selfish.

42
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,160
Come on, let's walk down together.

43
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:47,560
If you really can't do it,

44
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:48,840
I'll carry you.

45
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,050
You definitely won't be scared in my arms.

46
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:53,160
It's okay.

47
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,440
There's another way down.

48
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:55,400
I'll take you.

49
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,160
Wait for me. I'll go with you.

50
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,160
Don't look if you're scared.

51
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,840
Do you have any team spirit left?

52
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,040
Let me reiterate.

53
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,039
Qingqing is no longer your employee,

54
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:10,440
so she doesn't need to follow your rules.

55
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,360
I'm timid too.

56
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,600
Since you guys are so manly,

57
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,860
go down by yourselves.

58
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,360
What do you mean?

59
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,600
Are you picking a fight?

60
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,360
Girls

61
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,520
always form cliques.

62
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:20,640
We men are brave.

63
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:21,960
I'll take the elevator with you.

64
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,360
I'm taking the elevator.

65
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,520
Seriously.

66
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,280
Going down.

67
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,240
Qingqing, thank you for just now.

68
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:40,960
It's nothing.

69
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,280
Everyone has things they are afraid of.

70
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,520
Some fears are innate.

71
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,600
You don't have to overcome them.

72
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,329
I have things I'm afraid of too.

73
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,520
Aren't you going with them?

74
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:55,800
It's fine. I haven't wanted
to be with them for a long time.

75
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,240
Finally got rid of those two bad apples.

76
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:01,360
Now the real team building has just begun.

77
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:01,840
Let's go.

78
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:02,480
Let's go.

79
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:03,960
Qingqing,

80
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,040
should we

81
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:07,040
send them a message to let them know?

82
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,920
Turn off all your phones.

83
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,080
When they ask,

84
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,400
just say they ran out of battery.

85
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,079
Just have fun. I'm turning mine off.

86
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,360
So pretty.

87
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,600
Three, two, one.

88
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:24,920
Cheese.

89
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:32,850
Come on, come on.

90
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,640
It's pretty here too, right?

91
00:03:40,079 --> 00:03:40,920
Come here.

92
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,040
Let's go.

93
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,000
Okay, let's go.

94
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,840
You look so handsome in this.

95
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,280
You can face this way.

96
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,000
I take better pictures.

97
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,280
One, two, three.

98
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:17,959
Hurry up.

99
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,600
Victory is right ahead.

100
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,620
Passengers on the edge
of the clouds, follow me.

101
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,360
What are you?

102
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,000
Captain Qingqing, right?

103
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:30,440
Slow down, slow down.

104
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:32,600
But I only have these small ones here.

105
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,600
Almost, almost. Don't drop it.

106
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:34,840
Don't drop it, don't drop it.

107
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,159
Go, go, go.

108
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:38,040
Over here, it's all streams.

109
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:40,240
We often skip stones here.

110
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,080
That's amazing.

111
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,200
I have a great harvest.

112
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,800
Doesn't it look like a sweet potato?

113
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,000
It looks a bit like a sweet potato.

114
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,720
Right? A roasted one.

115
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,720
This one will definitely burn well.

116
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,100
Can even girls skip stones this well?

117
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,120
That's really great.

118
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,440
I'll sing one then.

119
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:57,600
You guys have to back me up.

120
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,680
You sing. Come on.

121
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,560
My lady.

122
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,800
Aha.

123
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,280
Cheers!

124
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,160
How about we record a video together?

125
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,080
Sure.

126
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,080
You film us. Come on.

127
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:12,680
I'll do it.

128
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:15,920
Make us look good.

129
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,980
Here we go. Come on.

130
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:21,900
Take a look.

131
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:22,920
Is it good? Is it good?

132
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:23,520
Let me see. Let me take a look.

133
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,450
I want to see too.

134
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,520
He shoots really well.

135
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,000
You're pretty good at this, Shen Feng.

136
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:28,600
Is it okay?

137
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,040
I have material for my Moments tonight.

138
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,080
Let's have another toast.

139
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,120
Come on. Let's do it.

140
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,400
Cheers! Cheers! Cheers!

141
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,080
The peanuts are edible too.

142
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:41,560
Here.

143
00:05:45,159 --> 00:05:46,800
Can you peel some more?

144
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:47,600
Okay.

145
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,920
I'll peel more for you.

146
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,400
Let me go check
if the sweet potatoes are ready.

147
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,000
Wait for me. I'll go with you.

148
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,159
Be careful. You must be careful.

149
00:05:55,159 --> 00:05:56,159
It's too dark now.

150
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,800
Don't go too far.

151
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:58,600
Okay.

152
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,320
It's so itchy.

153
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,520
Stop scratching.

154
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,360
Here, let me see.

155
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:10,480
Your leg is swollen from mosquito bites.

156
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,940
Didn't you feel it all day?

157
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,880
I was probably too happy today to notice.

158
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:17,600
I'd better do it myself.

159
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:19,580
Sit still. Don't move.

160
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,159
Thank you.

161
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:37,200
Qingqing seems much happier
since she quit.

162
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,880
Looks like she found her Mr. Right too.

163
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,920
She's happy again.

164
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,850
Chef Shen definitely
treats Qingqing differently.

165
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,800
Bear with it.

166
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,400
It'll be fine once I apply this.

167
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:50,000
I'm trying. It's really itchy.

168
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,560
Almost done. Almost done.

169
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,480
Does applying the ointment like this work?

170
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,920
You're just pressing a cross
on the mosquito bite.

171
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,480
It'll be fine soon.

172
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,440
It'll be fine once I apply this.

173
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,400
N-No.

174
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,400
I-I'm sorry.

175
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,800
I didn't mean to.

176
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,600
It's okay. I deserved it.

177
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,600
Be good. It'll be done soon.

178
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:12,840
What are you smiling at?

179
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:13,760
Nothing.

180
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,640
I'm just really, really happy.

181
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,440
Shen Feng,

182
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,720
I think I really love it here.

183
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,440
I love the scenery here,

184
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,600
the stories here,

185
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,730
and the people here.

186
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,960
Does that include me?

187
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:28,960
Of course.

188
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,360
And Shu Rong,

189
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:33,720
Shan Chuan, and Huo Huo,

190
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,320
and Tang Bao, and...

191
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:37,880
Playing dumb again.

192
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,400
You know what I mean.

193
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,480
The sweet potatoes over there seem ready.

194
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,340
Let's eat them while they're hot.

195
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,080
Okay.

196
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,600
It's okay.

197
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,320
I'll wait for you.

198
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,720
The sweet potato is too hot.

199
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,980
I'll go peel it for you.

200
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,100
Be good and wait for me.

201
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:20,320
I was a bit too emotional last night.

202
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,160
I'm sorry.

203
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:24,400
It's okay.

204
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,930
I didn't take your feelings into account.

205
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,040
Actually, to some extent,

206
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,799
I quite envy you.

207
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,280
Alright, stop thinking
about those unhappy things.

208
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:37,480
Let me show you the photos we took today.

209
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,039
I just looked at them. They look great.

210
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:44,039
This... this is so pretty.

211
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:44,720
Right?

212
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,440
Look, look.

213
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,240
You were scared of heights then.

214
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:06,840
What did you do yesterday?

215
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,280
You kept us waiting for so long.

216
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,560
Do you have any manners?

217
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:11,360
You didn't even send a message.

218
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,560
Calm down, calm down.

219
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,000
My phone died yesterday.

220
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,120
Your phone died?

221
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,760
I was talking about her, not you, right?

222
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:19,560
Yun Qingqing,

223
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,600
you're our team guide,

224
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:23,440
but you just left us behind.

225
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,520
Is that appropriate?

226
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,760
We should have been taking our time,

227
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:29,220
but instead we were rushing
and scrambling.

228
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,360
You've been out of the job for so long,

229
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,690
yet your work attitude is still so sloppy.

230
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:44,760
I've been talking for ages,

231
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:47,120
and you don't even know
to pour me a cup of tea?

232
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,920
Can't you pour it yourself?

233
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:50,880
Since when are you disabled?

234
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:53,800
Is she talking to me?

235
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,420
You think she's talking to me?

236
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,280
Submissive at home,

237
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:00,800
but acting like a boss

238
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,650
and throwing your weight around outside.

239
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:04,960
Hu Yuqian,

240
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,600
is that how you talk to your elders?

241
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,920
Believe it or not, I'll call your mom.

242
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:09,760
Call her.

243
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:10,960
I'll dial the number for you. Come on.

244
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:11,880
I'll use my phone. Stop.

245
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,210
Where's my phone? Stop.

246
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,040
Mr. Hu, Yuqian might be on her period

247
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,000
and in a bad mood.

248
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:20,760
Hu Yuqian,

249
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:22,880
with this attitude of yours...

250
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:24,360
I'm the only one who puts up with you.

251
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,920
Try working anywhere else.

252
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,840
You'd have been fired long ago.

253
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,440
Perfect. Let me tell you,

254
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,240
I'm done. I quit.

255
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,680
You think this company is your home?

256
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:33,120
Coming and going as you please?

257
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,780
You need to go through
the procedures to resign.

258
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,040
What are you doing?

259
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,000
I'm not here to negotiate.

260
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,320
I'm informing you.

261
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,040
This is

262
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,880
outrageous!

263
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,640
Where's my phone? I...

264
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,400
Mr. Hu, I'm calling your dad.

265
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,080
Bro, waiting for food?

266
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,280
Hu,

267
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:02,600
you were so badass just now.

268
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,360
You roasted your uncle so hard

269
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:06,360
he almost passed out.

270
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:08,380
How did you suddenly get so brave?

271
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:12,880
I just suddenly figured some things out.

272
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,480
If my life is on a countdown,

273
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:20,160
I really don't want
to waste another second

274
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:22,320
on toxic people and drama.

275
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:23,400
If

276
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,720
I die tomorrow,

277
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:28,970
I definitely don't want
to compromise myself today.

278
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:35,800
Where are you?

279
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,360
I want to see you.

280
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:40,480
Okay.

281
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,840
Am I being too impulsive?

282
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:50,840
Go on.

283
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,120
Thank you.

284
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,200
Where are you going?

285
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:12,960
You're never home,

286
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,560
leaving me in this empty house.

287
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:15,520
I have to work.

288
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:18,000
Didn't you just get off work?

289
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:19,720
I deliver food part-time at night.

290
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:20,880
Then I'll go with you.

291
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:21,520
I gotta go.

292
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,700
Delivering food isn't a game.

293
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:24,800
It's exhausting.

294
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,240
I'm so bored being home alone every day.

295
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,640
Just let me go with you.

296
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:31,360
You'd better wait for me at home.

297
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,040
I'm off.
